    "review": [
      "Both callers obtain masks through the complete CacheKey; the job snapshot normalizes only position before comparing seed, profile, storage bounds and exact parameter bits.",
      "Reuse requires the same tile origin, side, full retained column length, mask origin/width and vertical bounds. Larger overlapping tiles are rejected; outer fallback availability remains identical.",
      "Fresh terrain validation stays ahead of direct cache reuse. Job reuse can only capture already-generated, validated aligned dependency tiles.",
      "Fresh and reused paths share the original bounded ColumnCache/CaveCache insertion code. Existing keys, FIFO limits and contains-key behavior are preserved.",
      "Snapshots hold the cave-cache lock only while collecting Arcs. Crop and cache publication occur after the lock is released. No map lock or initializer waits on a recursive terrain producer.",
      "Snapshot selection is limited to the existing 64 nearby slots and excludes tiles completely covered by the initial field. The unbounded job fallback and initial-field precedence remain unchanged.",
      "Shared immutable mask ownership lasts until job retirement; no new global cache or background cleanup is introduced.",
      "Profiles without both patch and material halos retain normal generation. Direct custom/stem full-region validation is run separately from eligible Nether/Overworld GPU parity.",
      "GPU parity checks full metadata and sampled guard/interior/outside material, biome and height queries over every Y. Full corpus NBT comparisons remain the acceptance proof for integrated output.",
      "No source-order, RNG, structure, lighting, compression or publication code changed. Held cycle41 tile sizing and cycle39 material-run prototypes are excluded."
    ],
