  "implementation": [
    "Reuse only patch/material-halo fields with identical tile geometry, crop and material-mask coverage, obtained through the complete world/seed/profile/bounds/parameter key.",
    "At job creation retain matching aligned 16-chunk tiles only within the existing 64 nearby slots. Exclude initial-field-covered tiles. Generate every cache miss normally.",
    "Retain immutable masks through global eviction; crop metadata only when the job actually needs a tile. Ownership ends with the job.",
    "Fresh and reused fields invoke the original bounded ColumnCache/CaveCache publication code. Existing capacities, key handling and insertion order are unchanged.",
    "Add opt-in exact-reuse, snapshot and job-retention counters; no feature, ordering, RNG, structure, lighting, serialization or cleanup changes."
  ],
  "observations": [
    "Four adjacent measured regions: baseline generates 33270 terrain chunks across 66 tiles; selected candidate generates 31432 across 64. Four retained dependency tiles are used, with identical 252043 anchors and 13975953 intermediate columns.",
    "Restoring normal query-cache publication removes one side7 query relative to job-v3, but two extra side7 queries remain versus baseline. Retained terrain reduces measured work by 5.52%; this is not a wall-time share.",
    "Selected 20-region main readback is 216730529.6 bytes per region versus 229368332.2 in preceding merged full run; GPU completions are 712 versus 739.",
    "Fresh baseline/direct/job repeats remain close on latency. The selected publication variant also remains above one second; no settled speedup is claimed.",
    "Main generation peak RSS is 2318073856 bytes versus 2265989120 in the fresh preceding repeat. Retention is bounded by existing nearby slots, but this does not establish sustained-memory acceptance."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "User deferred quiet timing confirmation. All timing and peak-memory observations remain provisional; no settled speedup, Overworld non-regression or sub-second acceptance is claimed.",
    "Final sustained-memory, 1/2/4/8-caller and portal/DH acceptance remain open.",
    "Only selected publication variant has the complete five-case and reverse-two-caller corpus. Earlier variants have narrower coverage and are preserved as experiments."
  ],
